lines=['# Warning repair — paired results, 2026-10-23','',verdict,'','Local candidate; unpublished. This stage repairs the two warning regressions and the baptism/baby-shower false warnings identified in `red-team-release/REPORT.md`. Earlier failed evidence, including the S072/S100 citation failures and unsafe suppression witnesses, remains unchanged.','','## Change and validation boundary','','Only the validator warning filter changed. Obligation phrases (`have/has/had to`, `need/needs to`, `are/is/be obliged/obligated to`) protect genuine requirement context across source anchors. Offer-delivery phrases veto personal suppression within mixed statements. Clearly personal baptism and baby-shower bodies can be excluded from hints when trusted and present only in Section 12. Clinical text, explicit procurement cues, unknown meetings and unresolved required context retain warnings; an explicit personal body heading can reset context. No filename-based classification or blanket warning deletion was introduced.','','The implementation from `def difference` onward is byte-identical to the reviewed validator: exact quotations including invisible characters, exact complete anchors, trusted per-ID exclusions, heading/order/coverage/continuation checks and rejection behavior remain intact. A warning is a review aid, not proof of semantic correctness. The six model knowledge files in each arm are unchanged from the previous reviewed candidate. New model differences therefore reflect fresh-run variability, not a new routing-prompt repair.','','## Frozen questions and sequence','','`questions.md` is byte-identical to commit bfdd812. Inputs, expected routing, warning controls and protocol were committed before the original baseline. The original ran A–E, W/X/Y/Z and the unchanged full RFP first, and its complete baseline was committed before applying the candidate filter. Rebuild then used the same sources/order, unchanged runners, gpt-6-astra medium, fresh sessions and exact recorded continuations. No tools, retries, best-of selection, output corrections or evaluator answers were supplied. Exact requests, events, commands, hashes and card equality are audited. Host system instructions are not controlled.','','W is a new synthetic combination; X/Y/Z repeat the prior red-team sources. These are disclosed regression tests, not unseen real-world validation or fresh Claude acceptance. The full source is the same 214 real TBRPC statements plus seven synthetic personal statements. Its expanded selected semantic matrix was frozen before this pair; it does not grade every possible semantic placement.','','## Q1–Q8','', '| Question | Original | Rebuild | Comparison |','|---|---|---|---|']
